′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n- **I.** $(1,-3)$\n- **II.** $(-4,-1)$\n- **III.** $(0,3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ is the same as counterclockwise rotation by the same angle. It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-{180}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-{180}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-4,-1),(0,3),(1,-3).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20f4ef93-3e7b-58ec-992e-3a62b12b74e2" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 180 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db9320cd-33fb-54ff-b093-2de578a16444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469254} {:answer/id #uuid "ff595c9c-3fd0-5391-9f50-a5ca8485884f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff595c9c-3fd0-5391-9f50-a5ca8485884f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "tr