pe/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cedf0fcc-98d4-596a-ad79-42e7fd62dfba" :question/math-academy-id "q-81818" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-5,1),(0,-4),(3,5).$  Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians about the origin?\n- **I.** $(4,0)$\n- **II.** $(-3,-5)$\n- **III.** $(-1,5)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{\\pi },$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{\\pi }$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(5,-1),(0,4),(-3,-5).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20f4ef93-3e7b-58ec-992e-3a62b12b74e2" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 180 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc15f59-c768-5320-9ec4-70f3d142b675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469266} {:answer/id #uuid "5187f972-9f94-5165-af76-273d295ea3ba" 