ea1c0825" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eca92846-b208-5714-9d9f-4947d539dbcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-81819" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(4,4),(-3,-3),(-1,7).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n- **I.** $(3,-3)$\n- **II.** $(-4,-4)$\n- **III.** $(1,-7)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{180}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-4,-4),(3,3),(1,-7).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Sets are Orthogonal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eec7f9d0-6840-5a0d-9763-9d79e17c960b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469272} {:answer/id #uuid "e17563c3-bef4-5de4-bfa8-3abc6787cdbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eec7f9d0-6840-5a0d-9763-9d79e17c960b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469272} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2536c2a-97f0-5d07-85f7-dac71d9a3595" :answer-field/key "U" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470248} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c791f35-ef8d-5d1b-ac20-4bba4ba088a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469274} {:answer/id #uuid "42ccffe9-aa3a-51d7-a314-a985b53a16d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c791f35-ef8d-5d1b-ac20-4bba4ba088a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469274} :answer-field/id #uuid "c20072e3-cac0-5e39-9977-109f479878d1" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470249} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff210b55-f992-57f3-b9b8-5b982205db1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469276} {:answer/id #uuid "9b795f5c-7553-5cf0-835e-232adb57839c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b795f5c-7553-5cf0-835e-232adb57839c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469277} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e0a6fc6-975c-5d4a-a9d1-779257288450" :answer-field/key "W" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e6a1e4f-2315-5270-b1fa-4652e5933f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-82396" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n- **U.** $U={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}$\n- **V.** $V={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- **W.** $W={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}},$\n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2},{w}_{3}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,\\,{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\,{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0.$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0.$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0,\\,{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0,\\,{w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-10-3+0=-13\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $U$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=-18-2=-20\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=2-1-1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=0-1+1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=0+1-1=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $W$ is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$W$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351422 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Sets are Orthogonal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be5862e6-b730-5e81-9ac1-5e844249d701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469278} {:answer/id #uuid "654dd76b-a128-5d4e-b986-b07234a9d3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "654dd76b-a128-5d4e-b986-b07234a9d3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469279} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c6dc41f-cfa7-5461-a976-ac251c6b54e5" :answer-field/key "U" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470251} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e4af0f3-7d42-5e9a-abb1-c42b4f5355c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469280} {:answer/id #uuid "bd22712f-03ea-5666-af1b-1402b2b37d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd22712f-03ea-5666-af1b-1402b2b37d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469281} :answer-field/id #uuid "24699510-dda2-5446-ac6e-65cc0cd53489" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470252} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ac75cde-6eb1-56e3-9185-ae7e5ed25b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469282} {:answer/id #uuid "66347df5-2c1c-5bb6-89a7-f5ea0bcdf181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ac75cde-6eb1-56e3-9185-ae7e5ed25b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469282} :answer-field/id #uuid "34b6086a-d4e7-5d21-9eec-909a989af9d6" :answer-field/key "W" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470253}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c7632fcb-d145-5958-9540-44c860cfa586" :question/math-academy-id "q-82397" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n- **U.** $U={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- **V.** $V={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- **W.** $W={[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}},$ \n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,\\,{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\,{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0.$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0.$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-1+3-1-1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=1+0-2+1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=-1+0+2-1=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthogonal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=2-1-1=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $V$ is orthogonal.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]=-15+24=9\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ and $V$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133781 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed5c8af7-e617-5e8c-be01-45a26eb17d4d" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Sets are Orthonormal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b974feb-5457-574d-a527-ebd86a5e5813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1