e values: $0,1,2,3,…$\n\n- Statement II does *not* describe a discrete random variable. Although its value is determined by the result of an experiment, the possible values are real numbers that cannot be listed in a sequence.\n\n- Statement III does *not* describe a discrete random variable. Although its value is determined by the result of an experiment, we cannot list the possible real-numbered values in a sequence.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b86558a-4c99-5ccb-a100-719692a056f4" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa2ffce0-c5cc-554a-a75d-f7f66e307022" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469344} {:answer/id #uuid "2fd1cd16-9c7a-5e67-8a4b-ad3fb5a96267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fd1cd16-9c7a-5e67-8a4b-ad3fb5a96267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469345} :answer-field/id #uuid "2deefe50-fa4a-5c15-95ab-7513eb632eff" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470284} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3b5e61a-6f21-54f7-8c97-19149ef432e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469346} {:answer/id #uuid "76a9d57b-a1a0-571d-82b1-1bb94720a47d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3b5e61a-6f21-54f7-8c97-19149ef432e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469346} :answer-field/id #uuid "39cf3fda-c568-5bb5-9436-22c7b9a4d7ee" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470285} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43e0892a-70ad-5bf8-a99c-fd5c6d0c1379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469348} {:answer/id #uuid "81a7ba05-ee60-58cd-a5a6-e1046165b2a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43e0892a-70ad-5bf8-a99c-fd5c6d0c1379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469348} :answer-field/id #uuid "81d9abd9-b8ca-5470-8dbb-280bbbd3ab7b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d05b255-e15a-5a84-a441-46629f916127" :question/math-academy-id "q-8394" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,0),(1,5),(2,3).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians about the origin?\n- **I.** $(-5,1)$\n- **II.** $(0,-2)$\n- **III.** $(2,-3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{\\pi /2},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(0,0),(-5,1),(-3,2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b86558a-4c99-5ccb-a100-719692a056f4" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3d3e243-980a-5443-b39f-968258eea1dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469350} {:answer/id #uuid "b293378d-5abc-5d1a-95f9-ffaf61440ffb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b293378d-5abc-5d1a-95f9-ffaf61440ffb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469351} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8a6f178-1ec1-54b0-8ab8-948072730c0e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470287} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "521c8f26-598c-5fe9-9ae9-e0dbe28c2a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469352} {:answer/id #uuid "0b1b5eaa-2de3-5c59-8e59-a21eb831a1a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident 