rix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(2,0),(0,-3),(0,0).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354275 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20f4ef93-3e7b-58ec-992e-3a62b12b74e2" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 180 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "713bf4d1-ab25-5361-9e9c-7d24f6109f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469356} {:answer/id #uuid "fca5df3a-3e5a-5e39-9a04-d3f319e7d84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fca5df3a-3e5a-5e39-9a04-d3f319e7d84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469357} :answer-field/id #uuid "00bfb755-07a7-5384-afe7-6f942d8cdae4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470290} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cedc26c-1cb4-5561-91be-d73dca72eab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/tex