.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "404cdbaf-9eb2-5b1a-bb37-f06578b6497c" :question/math-academy-id "q-87155" :question/problem "Which of the following are continuous random variables?\n- **I.** The score when a roulette wheel is spun at random\n- **II.** The amount of water consumed by a randomly selected person on a particular day, measured in liters\n- **III.** The number of students in a particular class on a randomly selected day\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nCommon examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/05/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible outcomes do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\n- Statement II describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $(0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement III does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible values are the integers $0,1,2,…,$ which do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354553 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105860 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ee39554-fd77-5e90-baa8-f9320ffc3398" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Continuous Random Variables Given in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fcd158f-0765-56e8-b041-dd94505fd45c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469470} {:answer/id #uuid "6137ddad-126b-5ef9-9fbb-8d97823116f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6137ddad-126b-5ef9-9fbb-8d97823116f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469471} :answer-field/id #uuid "da62fcc9-8263-53b0-9ca4-0c17619b7b70" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470347} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acbd5c91-e836-59e8-ae65-b3f37cdf9027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469472} {:answer/id #uuid "5f3c9939-6250-551a-9971-3eee545fffcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acbd5c91-e836-59e8-ae65-b3f37cdf9027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469472} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cd118f3-de6e-55dd-b198-bc96bc67fea7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470348} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f6c02ab-e4d5-57bc-a091-d2e4911aee4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469474} {:answer/id #uuid "46a2b534-d795-53cb-89c0-b257103e5356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46a2b534-d795-53cb-89c0-b257103e5356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469475} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d6e2154-d58b-586e-a921-63d267d916c2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34701839-8ff2-5e14-88d5-939b8e4e71de" :question/math-academy-id "q-87160" :question/problem "Which of the following are continuous random variables?\n- **I.** The volume of milk produced by a particular cow on a randomly selected day, measured in liters\n- **II.** The outcome of rolling a $6$-sided die\n- **III.** The distance that a randomly selected runner can run in $30$ minutes\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nCommon examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/05/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real numbers in the interval $(0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible values are the integers $1,2,3,…,6,$ which do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\n- Statement III describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real numbers in the interval $(0,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354632 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157397 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3a247336-9bc8-5799-9956-e3de188ce2d2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Integrals That Evaluate to Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4290d91-204d-56a0-9987-3c5e660b7bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469476} {:answer/id #uuid "7edb0a43-f3f2-57e9-aabb-7339e723844c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7edb0a43-f3f2-57e9-aabb-7339e723844c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469477} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f4405f6-a235-58a4-9c4d-f1c15efcb26c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470350} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "942baa87-51cf-5c27-bbe2-b4d72e9a1c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469478} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca043e7-9abf-5a74-ad98-784c787973ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "942baa87-51cf-5c27-bbe2-b4d72e9a1c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469478} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a0c8103-5b3e-5f3b-98cc-6c07404b52bb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470351} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5228a88-de94-53c9-8036-7395a8d03a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469480} {:answer/id #uuid "dd9cb4a1-c8af-5b14-8e4c-5217af5953bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd9cb4a1-c8af-5b14-8e4c-5217af5953bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469481} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7bc4848-1177-5718-82e6-6482054cb9b1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02a56550-64c7-56dd-a9e8-7fca3f195d30" :question/math-academy-id "q-88208" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-5}^{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-2}^{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to zero due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡((-x)^{2}) \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-f(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+1)$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =(-x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-x+1) \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1-x) \\\\  & \\ne -g(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)={x}^{3}-2x$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-x) & =(-x)^{3}-2(-x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}+2x \\\\  & =-({x}^{3}-2x) \\\\  & =-h(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354654 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157397 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3a247336-9bc8-5799-9956-e3de188ce2d2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Integrals That Evaluate to Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44cdd7ee-61ad-5938-93f0-340f091e13f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469482} {:answer/id #uuid "2bdca250-cb7c-59e2-8ea4-8682367b7687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44cdd7ee-61ad-5938-93f0-340f091e13f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469482} :answer-field/id #uuid "56a40e4d-8106-5c75-b603-169710891875" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470353} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53d81538-ca99-5b08-9638-204451c7b66d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469484} {:answer/id #uuid "90b10bca-840e-519e-8eb8-431a9966008b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53d81538-ca99-5b08-9638-204451c7b66d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469484} :answer-field/id #uuid "a165ae9a-dab8-5535-8ea8-37b5c150931d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470354} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65aee6b8-9170-5390-9af5-9e119052d466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469486} {:answer/id #uuid "db143423-4313-5997-a91e-0fe80488518d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db143423-4313-5997-a91e-0fe80488518d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469487} :answer-field/id #uuid "0810f300-441d-560e-bef7-e416184b61d6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470355}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ebd12802-ac6e-5b21-a42e-2abc0f87cbb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-88689" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-4}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-2}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to $0$ due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3(-x)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) \\\\  & \\ne -f(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ is an odd function, but integral II is not of the form ${\\int }_{-a}^{a}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ since the upper and lower limits are not opposites. Therefore, we cannot use symmetry to simplify the integral.\n\n- The function $h(x)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-x) & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\  & =-h(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157397 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3a247336-9bc8-5799-9956-e3de188ce2d2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Integrals That Evaluate to Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "528a789d-e9c7-5c1e-bede-584c406a35b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469488} {:answer/id #uuid "767838c1-b861-5d59-84d8-031afa582bf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "767838c1-b861-5d59-84d8-031afa582bf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469489} :answer-field/id #uuid "46a94b13-a5ea-5b57-ad66-c14e58cfc1c0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "992eb133-179b-5758-ac35-c310625dc8b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469490} {:answer/id #uuid "75021ee1-aa2c-5619-8bda-64cfea23e945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75021ee1-aa2c-5619-8bda-64cfea23e945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469491} :answer-field/id #uuid "90749d04-f022-5ba8-b14c-931f696f7c64" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470357} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c103791-dc71-590e-b795-8db0963ef2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469492} {:answer/id #uuid "a779fe11-0f87-5bed-b6c5-622e15ea060f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c103791-dc71-590e-b795-8db0963ef2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469492} :answer-field/id #uuid "48cd5ea8-f344-59a6-ae82-9026baabb5dd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6956ed56-9d47-53cf-b35c-82d26f52b6fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-88692" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-2}^{2}x({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to zero due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(-x)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x) \\\\  & =-f(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=x({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =(-x)({e}^{(-x)}+{e}^{-(-x)}) \\\\  & =-x({e}^{-x}+{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =-x({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =-g(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{2}x({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-x) & =(-x)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(-x)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) \\\\  & \\ne -h(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354656 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157397 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3a247336-9bc8-5799-9956-e3de188ce2d2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Integrals That Evaluate to Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3a62b3e-3778-50e2-9b13-fca56d3109e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469494} {:answer/id #uuid "e76ffc94-1183-5bdc-a881-050b7728a4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e76ffc94-1183-5bdc-a881-050b7728a4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469495} :answer-field/id #uuid "db3bd7f9-0127-5cc0-9031-fc491225923b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470359} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eca809b4-79bc-5702-837b-f795e104c492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469496} {:answer/id #uuid "1337aa00-6b54-5794-8a95-c261410543b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eca809b4-79bc-5702-837b-f795e104c492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469496} :answer-field/id #uuid "95092969-3f5d-5977-baff-eeb5af76e796" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470360} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7521864a-802d-5ffe-ae58-df8224f7e2cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469498} {:answer/id #uuid "53549473-7f25-5327-bb42-de392cec6ca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7521864a-802d-5ffe-ae58-df8224f7e2cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469498} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d6887a1-1995-544d-b8ac-23ca51bdadaa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "857f38ae-b398-5bec-99e3-9572a98abf10" :question/math-academy-id "q-88695" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-7}^{7}x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-4}^{4}{x}^{2}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-2}^{2}(x+1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to zero due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)=x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x){e}^{-(-x)^{2}} \\\\  & =-x{e}^{-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-f(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-7}^{7}x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{x}$  is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =(-x)^{2}{e}^{(-x)} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{e}^{-x} \\\\  & \\ne -g(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)=(x+1)^{3}$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-x) & =((-x)+1)^{3} \\\\  & =(1-x)^{3} \\\\  & \\ne -h(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157397 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3a247336-9bc8-5799-9956-e3de188ce2d2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Integrals That Evaluate to Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7f7cf18-38f0-5077-a538-342af76dc308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469500} {:answer/id #uuid "06283436-a33a-58b7-a43f-b43074424d0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7f7cf18-38f0-5077-a538-342af76dc308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469500} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d12fdd3-bb32-5a4d-a689-b2163aa9260c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470362} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15309a98-2249-5a8f-8836-e83448833169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469502} {:answer/id #uuid "558b83bf-f917-545e-abd3-673c89b7308d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "558b83bf-f917-545e-abd3-673c89b7308d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469503} :answer-field/id #uuid "30c76670-dff0-51bc-9765-8c3d9cb1e80c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470363} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2e0d0a3-7248-5080-a257-664102b7609f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469504} {:answer/id #uuid "d63ff98e-39aa-52d8-a345-3c9ecc2a799f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2e0d0a3-7248-5080-a257-664102b7609f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469504} :answer-field/id #uuid "493d5107-b668-56d5-b4f0-5cd63321224a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ea94d170-9b47-53c8-b5f9-b4a6837f2064" :question/math-academy-id "q-88698" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}-2)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{5}+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to zero due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $h(x)={x}^{3}-2$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-x) & =(-x)^{3}-2 \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-2 \\\\  & =-({x}^{3}+2) \\\\  & \\ne -h(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $f(x)={x}^{5}+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{5}+(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{5}-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =-({x}^{5}+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =-f(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{5}+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{{x}^{2}})$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{(-x)^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & \\ne -g(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357387 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f7256c7-afea-5c33-a859-623b0531e88c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd0cb9d0-7a4e-5cee-9670-8ecef5397953" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469506} {:answer/id #uuid "b64c35dc-577d-5453-8511-098dfe72985a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd0cb9d0-7a4e-5cee-9670-8ecef5397953" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469506} :answer-field/id #uuid "af4da1b0-0dc1-5e61-9fd7-ab1709d5923a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470365} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a4f1d4a-05d0-5f02-8d12-8843949c13e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469508} {:answer/id #uuid "8aae8d9d-9a3b-539e-a8ec-80316c817815" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8aae8d9d-9a3b-539e-a8ec-80316c817815" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469509} :answer-field/id #uuid "66243b5a-3332-558d-9faa-1d5ba7ed36be" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470366} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4531a54d-3a0a-541c-93d0-00fa8344d8ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469510} {:answer/id #uuid "a745cba0-7f6d-5348-b9be-70cd6706fbe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4531a54d-3a0a-541c-93d0-00fa8344d8ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469510} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f9a935f-0519-58e4-bd89-3b8ce4602ea9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "89d077ef-e867-5965-84f4-b7f7051e5ef3" :question/math-academy-id "q-89206" :question/problem "Which of the following are discrete random variables?\n- **I.** The exact time (not rounded to integers) that a full charge of a phone battery lasts\n- **II.** The number of pets owned by a randomly selected family in a town\n- **III.** The height of a randomly selected plant in a nursery\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment.\n\nA *discrete* random variable is a random variable\n\n- that has finitely many possible values, or\n\n- whose possible values can be listed in a sequence: ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},…$\n\nRemember that a real interval (e.g. $(a,b)$ or $[a,b]$) cannot be listed in a sequence.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I does not describe a discrete random variable. Although its value is determined by the result of an experiment, the possible values are real numbers that cannot be listed in a sequence.\n\n- Statement II describes a discrete random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and it has finitely many possible values: $0,1,2,3,….$\n\n- Statement III does not describe a discrete random variable. Although its value is determined by the result of an experiment, the possible values are real numbers that cannot be listed in a sequence.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357392 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "162690db-70b3-54a8-a920-576a484a42d9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Binomial Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02d429a9-d70c-57e7-955e-30fdddf6b515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469512} {:answer/id #uuid "238e6910-c921-5791-8270-d2f8ece14bf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "238e6910-c921-5791-8270-d2f8ece14bf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469513} :answer-field/id #uuid "f114d1c5-53d1-5be4-8a50-b27e80bfcc02" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470368} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51b0c465-adbd-5ff2-a9f0-3672be3892ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469514} {:answer/id #uuid "bf5704a2-b5a2-5ba2-b7c6-d501f6aec86e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf5704a2-b5a2-5ba2-b7c6-d501f6aec86e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469515} :answer-field/id #uuid "5aa540f6-ffac-5aab-86d8-61a63849afb3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470369} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fff5b7d-5579-5929-a43d-471552870083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469516} {:answer/id #uuid "9fea0e66-c012-585b-8f4c-f437e1d53543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fff5b7d-5579-5929-a43d-471552870083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469516} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9ce6a27-7a10-5485-8403-ce9eac9b4de2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3640d184-7917-5cae-8823-08846078aa32" :question/math-academy-id "q-89354" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled as a binomial distribution?\n- **I.** The number of baskets made by a basketball player attempting three free throws if the probability of scoring any free throw is $65%$\n- **II.** The number of defective items in a random sample of $100$ items produced by a machine\n- **III.** The number of views of a video on a popular video channel\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binomial distribution models the number of successes in a sequence of $n$ independent experiments (where each outcome is either success or failure).\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of baskets in $3$ throws can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $3$ independent experiments.\n\n- Random variable II could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of defective items in a random sample of $100$ items can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $100$ independent experiments.\n\n- Random variable III could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of views cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "162690db-70b3-54a8-a920-576a484a42d9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Binomial Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e93a2454-b29e-51aa-80f3-9456b9873106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469518} {:answer/id #uuid "dd5a0f89-3a03-544b-ab65-85fa190c2574" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd5a0f89-3a03-544b-ab65-85fa190c2574" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469519} :answer-field/id #uuid "f10e36c2-2dc3-5a8c-903b-6074050e94dd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f3998e0-6302-5c52-8a19-fe98044b253b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469520} {:answer/id #uuid "e5745fe8-4932-5d7b-842e-a1d2946a921d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f3998e0-6302-5c52-8a19-fe98044b253b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469520} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0a804be-5a02-5859-b943-512a41d72c82" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470372} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a073217-e81a-5c33-ab4c-3c8b626fddb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469522} {:answer/id #uuid "6db41dbd-b851-55a5-814a-b51eebdc9862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a073217-e81a-5c33-ab4c-3c8b626fddb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469522} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7a5c00f-ebfa-5a2d-b8c3-bff6f593dde9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ad260dd3-b7b0-51a7-8aee-33250f0e09b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-89355" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled as a binomial distribution?\n- **I.** The number of boys in a family of $3$ children\n- **II.** The number of red cars passing through an avenue in an hour\n- **III.** The number of pizzas sold by a pizzeria in a day\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binomial distribution models the number of successes in a sequence of $n$ independent experiments (where each outcome is either success or failure).\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of boys can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $3$ independent experiments.\n\n- Random variable II could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. Although being red can be interpreted as a \"success,\" there is not a fixed number of trials in this experiment.\n\n- Random variable III could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of pizzas sold cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357424 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157363 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5586c38-e0ca-5a6d-90ab-71c0fead2cc2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Point on a Solution Curve Is a Stationary Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed391fce-2afe-5b9b-a9c6-f670b8630cb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469524} {:answer/id #uuid "57050e23-17df-5843-b160-7621d5528ccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed391fce-2afe-5b9b-a9c6-f670b8630cb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045